<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary/80 font-medium italic mb-8 border-l-4 border-secondary pl-6">A dentist (BDS) handles teeth, gums, and routine oral health — check-ups, fillings, cleanings, crowns, and simple extractions. A maxillofacial surgeon (MDS in Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery) is trained for surgical problems of the face, jaws, mouth, and neck — impacted wisdom teeth, jaw fractures, <a href="what-is-orthognathic-surgery.php" class="font-semibold text-secondary">orthognathic surgery</a>, oral cancer, cysts, and facial trauma. See a dentist first for everyday dental problems. See a maxillofacial surgeon when the problem is structural, surgical, or beyond routine dentistry.</p>
