<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Is a maxillofacial surgeon more expensive than a dentist?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">For complex procedures, yes — but specialist care often prevents bigger costs later. Simple dental work should always start with a dentist.</p></details>
